WEBVTT

00:07.007 --> 00:09.342
Three minutes remaining in Round 13.

00:24.149 --> 00:25.650
I couldn't care less about you.

01:39.349 --> 01:40.308
Damn!

01:45.313 --> 01:47.690
Two people remaining until checkmate.

01:51.069 --> 01:51.986
Lady?

02:01.621 --> 02:04.290
Everyone's more concerned
about their own lives than that kid

02:04.374 --> 02:07.669
and has joined the Queen Team.

02:11.422 --> 02:14.551
Nobody wants to kill a child, but…

02:16.010 --> 02:19.180
it's different
when your own life's on the line.

02:19.264 --> 02:22.016
We value our own lives over others'.

02:22.767 --> 02:24.936
That's the way we humans are.

02:28.064 --> 02:29.065
I can tell…

02:31.234 --> 02:33.653
you've never known anyone

02:34.821 --> 02:36.573
who was precious to you.

02:43.830 --> 02:47.500
I despise hypocrites like you.

02:51.588 --> 02:55.008
If this kid's that important to you,
then die together.

02:56.509 --> 02:57.594
But I know

02:59.637 --> 03:02.473
that you'll change your mind
sooner or later.

03:03.725 --> 03:04.726
You'll see.

03:18.448 --> 03:19.324
Are you okay?

03:22.243 --> 03:23.119
I swear

03:24.913 --> 03:26.581
I'll keep you alive.

03:30.126 --> 03:33.671
Round 14, the Challenger Team's turn,
will now commence.

03:34.839 --> 03:36.549
The round lasts for five minutes.

03:38.593 --> 03:39.469
Start.

04:54.210 --> 04:55.044
Usagi!

04:55.670 --> 04:56.671
Wait there!

05:04.262 --> 05:05.263
Are you okay?

05:05.763 --> 05:07.765
I've got an idea. Come with me.

05:11.019 --> 05:12.061
Ow!

05:31.622 --> 05:33.041
- Are you okay?
- Any sign of them?

05:34.500 --> 05:36.836
Not much time left.

05:37.462 --> 05:38.338
Run!

05:48.097 --> 05:51.517
Usagi, we need at least five more.
There's a bunch upstairs.

05:51.601 --> 05:53.019
- Let's go!
- Wait!

05:53.519 --> 05:55.229
We've got to hurry! There's no time!

05:55.313 --> 05:56.355
Wait.

06:04.989 --> 06:09.744
Do you guys really want
to be on the Queen Team and win?

06:11.287 --> 06:12.747
You're damn right.

06:13.623 --> 06:14.707
I don't want to die.

06:15.666 --> 06:19.712
If we're on the Queen Team and win,
we can stay here forever.

06:20.254 --> 06:23.132
Then we won't have to
participate in other games,

06:24.008 --> 06:25.760
and we won't get shot at all the time.

06:26.344 --> 06:29.806
Isn't there something more important
than winning this game?

06:29.889 --> 06:31.974
Right now, winning this game
is what's important!

06:34.185 --> 06:35.686
You're all wrong.

06:38.606 --> 06:39.524
Right now,

06:40.733 --> 06:44.821
what's most important
isn't winning this game.

06:47.990 --> 06:49.617
It's returning to the real world.

06:54.413 --> 06:56.666
If you're only worried
about winning the game

06:57.500 --> 07:00.461
and then do as the tough Queen says,
you'll probably win.

07:01.045 --> 07:03.881
And you may be able to survive
in this world forever.

07:06.175 --> 07:07.802
But is that what you want?

07:09.387 --> 07:12.098
If our team wins and we defeat the Queen,

07:12.181 --> 07:14.767
as well as all the face cards,

07:15.726 --> 07:19.397
we might be able to
return to the real world.

07:23.443 --> 07:26.237
There's no way in hell
we'll be able to go back.

07:27.822 --> 07:28.906
That other world

07:30.741 --> 07:32.410
has ended.

07:33.077 --> 07:35.413
The games always follow their rules.

07:36.873 --> 07:39.959
When the face cards lose, they're killed.

07:40.793 --> 07:43.546
So if we defeat all the face cards,

07:44.422 --> 07:46.007
these games will end for sure.

07:47.133 --> 07:48.551
There are no games after that.

07:50.386 --> 07:52.722
That's just your fantasy.

07:54.056 --> 07:54.974
Maybe so.

07:55.850 --> 07:56.684
But…

07:58.394 --> 08:02.398
the only people who survive
are the ones who hold onto that hope.

08:04.192 --> 08:06.777
Even if you can continue
to survive here with the Queen,

08:07.528 --> 08:08.779
it just means

08:10.198 --> 08:13.451
you live forever in this game
where you're killing each other!

08:17.663 --> 08:18.581
If you don't want that…

08:21.876 --> 08:23.377
then take a chance with us.

08:30.009 --> 08:32.512
This place is a lot like the real world.

08:35.515 --> 08:37.850
Do you really want to return
to the real world that badly?

08:40.019 --> 08:41.020
That place…

08:42.939 --> 08:44.273
totally sucked.

08:46.150 --> 08:48.152
I think this place
might actually be better.

08:59.372 --> 09:00.373
I'll admit,

09:02.375 --> 09:04.126
until now, I thought that way.

09:06.379 --> 09:08.881
The real world may not be a bed of roses.

09:12.885 --> 09:13.803
But…

09:16.597 --> 09:18.474
I want to go back.

09:23.521 --> 09:25.773
I want to go back to the real world.

09:29.735 --> 09:31.904
Even though it was full of pain,

09:34.574 --> 09:36.325
it was the world that gave me life

09:38.452 --> 09:40.329
and raised me.

09:42.290 --> 09:43.541
I miss it.

09:48.504 --> 09:50.339
It's a cold and lonely place,

09:54.927 --> 09:56.846
but because of my life there,

09:58.723 --> 09:59.974
I was able to discover

10:01.601 --> 10:03.853
the kindness in people here.

10:08.691 --> 10:10.693
I'd forgotten about that until now.

10:19.201 --> 10:20.286
I want to go back…

10:23.205 --> 10:25.041
and start over again there.

10:41.307 --> 10:42.433
I…

10:44.018 --> 10:45.019
want to go back.

10:49.398 --> 10:50.358
I also…

10:52.151 --> 10:53.152
want go back.

10:53.986 --> 10:54.904
I want to go back…

10:56.322 --> 10:57.698
and be with my family.

11:15.549 --> 11:16.550
Do you think

11:18.761 --> 11:20.137
I can also start over again?

11:25.476 --> 11:27.603
There are two rounds remaining.

11:28.187 --> 11:32.441
Round 15, the Queen Team's final turn,
will now commence.

11:33.109 --> 11:34.944
The round lasts for five minutes.

11:35.027 --> 11:35.945
Start.

12:02.972 --> 12:04.807
There are 14 of them.

12:04.890 --> 12:06.809
To gain a majority,
we'll need to take back five.

12:07.560 --> 12:09.311
That won't be easy in just one turn.

12:09.395 --> 12:11.730
And they can win just by running away.

12:11.814 --> 12:14.442
We'll just have to
go after them one by one.

12:15.693 --> 12:16.527
No.

12:22.408 --> 12:23.659
There's another way.

12:30.166 --> 12:33.586
I swear I'll get that guy
on my team before the end.

12:34.336 --> 12:35.546
What about the woman?

12:38.716 --> 12:39.800
We don't need her.

12:41.510 --> 12:44.763
I'll show her
that hypocrisy is pointless in this land.

12:45.723 --> 12:47.641
- Let's go!
- Come on!

13:15.419 --> 13:16.253
Over there!

13:17.588 --> 13:19.006
- We'll get you!
- Stop!

13:27.223 --> 13:29.016
We don't need you. Get out of the way!

13:34.188 --> 13:35.314
Wait! Go after her!

13:40.653 --> 13:42.530
- This way!
- All right!

13:53.415 --> 13:54.250
Go up!

14:00.256 --> 14:01.173
He's over there!

14:03.217 --> 14:04.051
There he is!

14:07.429 --> 14:08.681
Stop right there!

14:21.235 --> 14:24.405
Round 15 will be ending soon.

14:24.989 --> 14:26.407
Thirty seconds remaining.

14:54.435 --> 14:55.561
The final round.

14:55.644 --> 14:56.770
Start.

14:57.730 --> 14:59.148
Go!

15:05.237 --> 15:06.530
Arisu!

15:11.076 --> 15:12.536
He went that way!

15:21.337 --> 15:22.880
- Yes! We did it!
- We did it!

15:45.027 --> 15:48.280
- Yes! We did it!
- Yahoo! We did it!

15:48.364 --> 15:50.115
Thank god! We did it!

15:50.199 --> 15:52.743
- Thank you!
- You too!

15:58.791 --> 15:59.875
Thank goodness.

16:06.382 --> 16:07.383
Lady.

16:19.520 --> 16:22.523
I don't know how you persuaded everyone,

16:23.440 --> 16:26.443
but well done, Miss Hypocrite.

16:29.113 --> 16:30.114
I simply

16:31.782 --> 16:35.369
want to get out of this land
with the people precious to me.

16:37.079 --> 16:37.955
That's all.

16:40.582 --> 16:41.625
Oh, really?

16:43.836 --> 16:46.255
We're a hell of a lot freer here.

16:47.715 --> 16:50.884
I like it here better
than in that rigid, repressive world.

16:52.511 --> 16:53.679
Just as I thought,

16:55.139 --> 16:59.309
you all were players like us
and have stayed in this world.

17:00.519 --> 17:01.812
Isn't that right?

17:05.441 --> 17:09.111
You'll find out
once all the games are over.

17:09.194 --> 17:10.279
When they're all over?

17:11.947 --> 17:14.033
What will we find out
when they're all over?

17:15.951 --> 17:20.956
You'll know the answer to that
only after you've cleared the last one.

17:22.291 --> 17:23.792
Will we know what this world is?

17:23.876 --> 17:25.544
Will we be able to go back?

17:29.298 --> 17:31.300
That's something
for you to look forward to.

17:33.052 --> 17:35.387
- Time has run out.
- Hey!

17:35.471 --> 17:39.475
The game is over
for all members of the Queen Team.

17:41.018 --> 17:43.687
I want to live free until the very end.

17:46.523 --> 17:47.566
Farewell.

18:37.199 --> 18:38.951
I want to finish these games fast

18:40.285 --> 18:41.703
and find out the answer.

18:44.957 --> 18:46.458
But I want to survive

18:48.210 --> 18:50.212
and return to the real world

18:53.048 --> 18:54.216
with you, Usagi.

19:00.597 --> 19:01.682
Me too.

19:14.278 --> 19:15.279
Hey, look at that.

19:25.289 --> 19:26.540
This smell…

19:29.042 --> 19:29.960
Did you fart?

19:30.794 --> 19:31.753
No.

20:16.173 --> 20:17.007
It's hot!

20:21.136 --> 20:23.430
Wow! It's a hot spring.

20:24.056 --> 20:25.349
This is a hot spring!

20:26.433 --> 20:27.309
Usagi!

20:27.851 --> 20:28.685
This is awesome!

20:28.769 --> 20:30.187
It's really a hot spring!

20:31.855 --> 20:33.190
The water is just right here!

20:33.732 --> 20:34.566
Seriously?

20:35.067 --> 20:36.109
Let's take a bath!

20:36.860 --> 20:38.570
I haven't had a bath in ages!

20:38.654 --> 20:39.988
We can't let this chance go!

20:41.490 --> 20:42.324
Together?

20:43.408 --> 20:45.577
What? Oh…

21:05.514 --> 21:07.849
You know, I wouldn't mind dying now.

21:12.479 --> 21:13.438
If only…

21:15.107 --> 21:17.693
we could wash away all the pain here too.

21:20.737 --> 21:21.655
That's for sure.

21:27.536 --> 21:28.370
What's wrong?

21:29.288 --> 21:30.122
Usagi?

21:32.708 --> 21:33.542
Usagi?

21:35.669 --> 21:36.586
Hey!

21:37.629 --> 21:38.797
Usagi!

21:42.968 --> 21:44.052
No way.

21:46.680 --> 21:47.681
Incredible.

22:07.659 --> 22:09.161
The elephants are bathing too.

22:11.788 --> 22:14.041
They must have escaped from the zoo.

22:17.419 --> 22:18.754
If we hadn't come to this land…

22:20.255 --> 22:21.673
We never would have seen this.

22:23.884 --> 22:24.843
Yeah.

22:28.597 --> 22:29.681
What's wrong with me?

22:30.932 --> 22:32.517
Suddenly, I feel

22:33.810 --> 22:35.812
incredibly moved.

22:40.567 --> 22:41.526
Me too.

22:59.294 --> 23:01.296
Sorry! I didn't see anything.

23:01.797 --> 23:05.092
I was looking at the elephants.
I'm only interested in them.

23:05.967 --> 23:06.802
I like elephants.

23:07.427 --> 23:08.261
It's okay.

23:11.098 --> 23:12.099
Stay here with me.

26:02.394 --> 26:03.687
There it is.

26:24.165 --> 26:26.751
KIMIKO KUINA
ADMITTED: JUNE 2, 2021

26:50.442 --> 26:51.776
I want to see you, Mom.

28:04.140 --> 28:06.309
She's so young. It's so heartbreaking.

28:07.977 --> 28:09.896
All the results
of disgusting human desires.

28:13.233 --> 28:15.235
Maybe there's no hope for this world.

28:17.320 --> 28:18.988
Even though she knew she'd die,

28:20.281 --> 28:22.617
she fought desperately until the end.

28:25.829 --> 28:27.330
She never gave up hope.

28:50.603 --> 28:52.021
I've still got hope.

29:23.803 --> 29:28.016
SUPREME COURT

29:44.032 --> 29:45.158
Well, well.

29:46.451 --> 29:48.661
So, you were the King of Diamonds.

29:49.662 --> 29:51.206
The former executive at the Beach

29:51.748 --> 29:55.168
and Number 2, Kuzuryu.

29:57.420 --> 30:00.590
Why was the King of Diamonds at the Beach?

30:03.301 --> 30:04.969
I was interested in it.

30:05.970 --> 30:07.222
You went undercover?

30:09.933 --> 30:11.976
Difficulty level, King of Diamonds.

30:12.060 --> 30:14.813
Game: Balance Scale.

30:17.690 --> 30:18.733
Shall we begin?

30:25.782 --> 30:27.951
BALANCE SCALE

30:34.791 --> 30:37.961
Rules: Within the three-minute time limit,

30:38.044 --> 30:42.090
select a number between 0 and 100.

30:42.966 --> 30:47.220
The average of the numbers chosen
is then multiplied by 0.8.

30:47.720 --> 30:51.766
The person who chooses
the number closest to this is the winner.

30:53.476 --> 30:56.563
The average of the numbers
that everyone selects

30:57.063 --> 30:58.648
is multiplied by 0.8.

31:00.358 --> 31:03.695
And whoever gets closest to it wins.

31:04.779 --> 31:09.242
What? Multiply the average by 0.8?

31:10.410 --> 31:13.413
Why multiply by 0.8? What's with 0.8?

31:14.289 --> 31:15.164
I get it.

31:16.374 --> 31:20.920
By multiplying by the constant 0.8,
it tips the balance of the scale.

31:22.422 --> 31:23.715
That's how it becomes a game.

31:24.757 --> 31:29.137
The 0.8 is like a drop from heaven.

31:30.847 --> 31:34.183
Everyone except for the winner
loses one point.

31:34.267 --> 31:36.352
Then the round ends.

31:37.020 --> 31:42.609
When a player reaches negative ten points,
the game is over for that player.

31:42.692 --> 31:46.487
The one person who survives
until the end is the victor.

31:46.988 --> 31:51.326
However, every time a player loses,
a new rule is introduced.

31:51.409 --> 31:54.245
New rules? What's with that?

31:57.206 --> 31:59.584
And no explanation
of the balance scales either?

32:01.544 --> 32:04.172
Round 1 will now start.

32:43.169 --> 32:45.421
Time has expired.

32:45.505 --> 32:47.340
Here are the results for Round 1.

32:49.384 --> 32:51.094
The average…

32:52.595 --> 32:54.597
is 32.8.

32:54.681 --> 32:57.600
This is multiplied by the constant 0.8.

32:57.684 --> 32:59.352
RESULT: 26.24

32:59.435 --> 33:02.438
This is the person who is closest.

33:03.398 --> 33:05.942
The winner is Kuzuryu.

33:12.699 --> 33:14.742
If everyone selects 40,

33:16.077 --> 33:18.162
the average will obviously be 40.

33:18.913 --> 33:21.958
When that's multiplied by 0.8,
it comes to 32.

33:22.709 --> 33:26.879
If everyone made
the same assumption and chose 32,

33:26.963 --> 33:29.298
the result will still be
multiplied by 0.8.

33:29.382 --> 33:33.428
As long as that happens,
the result will continue to decrease.

33:34.470 --> 33:37.056
Even if everyone chooses the same number,

33:38.975 --> 33:40.393
there won't be a winner.

33:40.977 --> 33:42.103
I get it now.

33:42.186 --> 33:46.649
We need to predict what everyone chooses
and then predict again even lower.

33:47.316 --> 33:50.278
This is actually more like a heart game.

33:51.362 --> 33:52.697
It's a psychological battle?

33:52.780 --> 33:56.826
Like chess, poker,
and all intellectual games,

33:56.909 --> 33:58.619
you have to read your opponent.

34:00.121 --> 34:03.875
But you don't read
your opponent psychologically.

34:04.542 --> 34:05.793
You read their logic.

34:08.296 --> 34:09.213
Isn't that right?

34:11.382 --> 34:12.341
Logic?

34:19.640 --> 34:20.641
You're ignoring me?

34:23.561 --> 34:24.479
What's that?

34:25.313 --> 34:26.147
Water?

34:30.318 --> 34:31.319
It's sulfuric acid.

34:31.944 --> 34:32.779
What?

34:32.862 --> 34:34.530
So, you'll answer
those kinds of questions.

34:36.032 --> 34:38.868
When you're at negative ten points,
the scale must tip.

34:40.328 --> 34:41.913
Your body will melt,

34:43.498 --> 34:45.541
and you'll turn to mush!

34:52.006 --> 34:53.257
Balance scales.

34:55.009 --> 35:00.348
That must mean
the King of Diamonds was a lawyer, huh?

35:02.266 --> 35:04.018
That's all in the past.

35:04.602 --> 35:05.645
So it's complicated.

35:06.771 --> 35:10.191
But you still chose this place.

35:11.567 --> 35:14.821
The arena for this game is a court.

35:16.823 --> 35:18.032
And these giant scales…

35:18.908 --> 35:22.829
Like the symbol on a lawyer's pin,
they represent fairness and equality.

35:23.788 --> 35:28.459
All lives have equal value,
including your own.

35:29.127 --> 35:30.336
Is that what you want to say?

35:32.797 --> 35:36.759
The scales always tip
to the side that has more gold.

35:38.553 --> 35:40.346
All lives don't have equal value.

35:44.809 --> 35:47.311
Round 2 will now start.

35:48.146 --> 35:50.815
The last result was 26.

35:50.898 --> 35:53.401
So if that's multiplied by 0.8…

35:53.985 --> 35:57.155
Wait. If everyone has the same idea,
I'd have to look farther ahead

35:57.238 --> 35:59.782
and multiply by 0.8 again.

36:00.575 --> 36:04.662
If everyone chooses 100,
multiply that by 0.8 and you get 80.

36:04.745 --> 36:07.206
There's no point
in ever choosing 80 or higher.

36:07.290 --> 36:10.918
If nobody will ever choose 80 or higher,
the highest average is 80.

36:11.002 --> 36:13.504
Multiply that by 0.8 and you get 64.

36:13.588 --> 36:15.715
If the highest average is 64,

36:15.798 --> 36:17.884
when you multiply that by 0.8,
you get 51.2.

36:17.967 --> 36:19.260
In other words, 51.

36:20.261 --> 36:23.347
The more steps you predict,
the closer the result gets to zero.

36:24.432 --> 36:28.561
In the stock market, everyone invariably
invests in the brands everyone wants.

36:29.312 --> 36:31.981
Now I just need to predict
what everyone will want.

36:32.064 --> 36:36.235
Predicting how many steps ahead
everyone else will predict

36:36.861 --> 36:38.446
is the key to this game.

36:39.071 --> 36:42.825
I've already developed the formula
for reading everyone's logic.

36:42.909 --> 36:44.785
Time has expired.

36:44.869 --> 36:46.245
Here are the results for Round 2.

36:46.329 --> 36:48.122
The average…

36:49.081 --> 36:50.541
is 16.6.

36:51.459 --> 36:54.253
This is multiplied by the constant 0.8.

36:54.337 --> 36:56.088
RESULT: 13.28

36:56.172 --> 36:58.883
This is the person who is closest.

36:59.634 --> 37:02.303
The winner is Kuzuryu.

37:16.484 --> 37:18.361
Everyone's gotten better at predicting.

37:20.071 --> 37:22.031
The numbers keep getting smaller.

37:22.615 --> 37:24.533
Should I just choose zero?

37:26.827 --> 37:30.081
By logical prediction,
the result converges to zero.

37:30.665 --> 37:32.541
Ultimately, everyone will choose zero.

37:34.627 --> 37:37.463
The most logical choice is to choose zero.

37:37.546 --> 37:41.968
But everyone's definition
of "logical" is different.

37:44.887 --> 37:45.846
Kuzuryu.

37:47.640 --> 37:48.557
What?

37:49.642 --> 37:51.394
I have a pretty good idea now…

37:52.561 --> 37:54.313
of what you're trying to measure.

37:57.108 --> 37:58.609
The value of life, right?

38:02.405 --> 38:03.322
No.

38:04.115 --> 38:05.449
So what is it?

38:06.784 --> 38:07.868
Tell me.

38:20.256 --> 38:22.842
What if we submit
another settlement figure?

38:23.843 --> 38:25.011
The truth is,

38:25.094 --> 38:28.723
twenty people living near the factory died
from the damage done to the environment

38:28.806 --> 38:31.142
caused by the waste
that the factory dumped.

38:31.225 --> 38:33.436
Their diseases
could have been caused by anything.

38:34.353 --> 38:36.897
Where's the proof
that our company is to blame?

38:39.900 --> 38:42.695
I heard that
you're an extremely talented lawyer,

38:42.778 --> 38:44.739
but you don't truly understand
the law, do you?

38:45.573 --> 38:49.702
The law doesn't exist
to protect the weak from the powerful.

38:50.286 --> 38:51.871
Everyone is equal under the law.

38:51.954 --> 38:53.164
That's absurd idealism!

38:56.334 --> 38:58.377
To save the starvation of the world,

38:58.878 --> 39:02.506
one needs the power to
effortlessly propel the world's economy.

39:03.049 --> 39:04.383
But with your idealism alone,

39:04.467 --> 39:07.178
this incredibly unfair world
can't be changed.

39:07.261 --> 39:08.346
So let me ask you this.

39:11.182 --> 39:13.851
What do you think we should do
in order to maintain

39:13.934 --> 39:16.145
a perfectly just modern society?

39:19.148 --> 39:23.527
We must make it possible, on every level,
to implement a fair judicial system.

39:24.737 --> 39:26.113
Just now,

39:26.197 --> 39:29.742
you said one needs the power to
effortlessly propel the world's economy.

39:30.493 --> 39:32.620
But by focusing only on
the growth of the economy,

39:32.703 --> 39:34.121
- the wealth gap has widen--
- Listen!

39:35.623 --> 39:39.335
As a lawyer,
it's not your duty to defend what's just.

39:39.418 --> 39:41.796
Even idiots can defend the just!

39:42.463 --> 39:46.884
Words like "fairness" and "equality"
are useless in a world filled with evil!

39:47.802 --> 39:50.930
However, when something isn't "just,"

39:51.597 --> 39:54.266
then it is your duty to use

39:55.017 --> 39:59.772
the gift of imagination
that God gave you to make it "just."

40:09.824 --> 40:11.826
Time has expired.

40:12.410 --> 40:14.370
Here are the results for Round 3.

40:17.498 --> 40:18.624
One hundred?

40:18.707 --> 40:21.293
The average is 20.2.

40:21.377 --> 40:24.130
This is multiplied by the constant 0.8.

40:24.213 --> 40:26.757
This is the closest person.

40:26.841 --> 40:28.592
The winner is Daimon.

40:29.176 --> 40:31.804
What? I won?

40:31.887 --> 40:32.721
Yes!

40:33.389 --> 40:34.432
Hey, you!

40:35.474 --> 40:36.809
What did you do that for?

40:37.435 --> 40:39.520
If you choose 100, you'll lose!

40:40.146 --> 40:42.731
There's a zero percent chance you'll win!

40:43.983 --> 40:46.735
Everyone's dissecting this a little
too meticulously, don't you think?

40:48.529 --> 40:50.698
That kind of thing
just makes my head hurt,

40:51.866 --> 40:53.200
so I decided to blow it up.

41:03.085 --> 41:04.753
You've lost your marbles.

41:07.423 --> 41:09.133
ROUND 6

41:09.717 --> 41:11.385
Here are the results for Round 6.

41:12.052 --> 41:13.888
The winner is Chishiya.

41:20.227 --> 41:21.896
Here are the results for Round 7.

41:22.396 --> 41:23.814
RESULT: 23.04

41:23.898 --> 41:26.400
The winner is Daimon.

41:29.862 --> 41:30.863
Yes!

41:38.787 --> 41:41.957
That sure won't be a pleasant way to die.

41:43.751 --> 41:45.377
ROUND 10

41:45.461 --> 41:47.796
I've only got one point left.

41:47.880 --> 41:49.548
If I get this one wrong, I'll die.

41:49.632 --> 41:51.926
I thought my formula was perfect!

41:57.431 --> 42:01.769
Oh, dear! I've got no idea what to do!
I can't use the same tricks again.

42:02.478 --> 42:04.355
I can't make any more wrong guesses!

42:05.147 --> 42:06.857
If I lose the next one, it's all over!

42:08.776 --> 42:12.988
If you think logically,
the numbers will get smaller and smaller.

42:16.742 --> 42:19.245
You must have predicted this would happen.

42:30.506 --> 42:32.341
Here are the results for Round 10.

42:32.424 --> 42:33.801
RESULT: 1.6

42:33.884 --> 42:36.345
The winner is Kuzuryu.

42:39.848 --> 42:42.893
There are participants
who have negative ten points.

42:48.232 --> 42:51.986
The game is over
for these two participants.

42:59.702 --> 43:02.079
Let me out of here!
Please! Let me out of here!

43:03.956 --> 43:05.583
No!

43:05.666 --> 43:06.959
Let me out!

43:07.042 --> 43:08.460
Hey! Let me out of this thing!

43:08.544 --> 43:09.628
I'll do anything you want!

43:10.212 --> 43:12.047
Is it money you want? Please!

43:12.965 --> 43:14.133
Tell me!

43:15.634 --> 43:17.344
- Let me out!
- I'll do anything you want!

44:10.731 --> 44:13.317
Now, this is more like a face card game.

44:14.902 --> 44:17.488
Is this what you call fairness?

44:19.990 --> 44:24.745
Since two participants lost,
two new rules will be added.

44:25.746 --> 44:29.583
Rule one: If two or more people
choose the same number,

44:29.667 --> 44:32.836
their choice will be invalidated
and they will lose one point.

44:33.629 --> 44:37.466
Rule two:
If the answer is guessed exactly,

44:37.549 --> 44:40.469
the losers will lose two points.

44:40.552 --> 44:43.347
ADDITIONAL RULES

45:08.122 --> 45:10.040
Here are the results for Round 11.

45:16.088 --> 45:17.756
Everybody chose zero…

45:18.674 --> 45:23.137
Since everyone chose the same number,
their choices are invalidated.

45:23.637 --> 45:25.764
Everyone loses one point.

45:25.848 --> 45:27.015
What?

45:27.099 --> 45:29.518
In the end, everyone chooses zero.

45:31.103 --> 45:34.857
If that happens again,
it's game over for me.

45:36.233 --> 45:37.151
ROUND 12

45:37.234 --> 45:39.862
Round 12 will now start.

45:50.372 --> 45:52.583
Here are the results for Round 12.

45:58.172 --> 46:01.383
RESULT: 22.93

46:02.968 --> 46:07.931
We have an exact winner,
so the losers lose two points.

46:12.102 --> 46:13.103
No way…

46:13.187 --> 46:15.939
No way! Impossible! How come?

46:17.399 --> 46:19.193
You saw my choice, didn't you?

46:19.276 --> 46:21.528
That's against the rules!

46:21.612 --> 46:24.656
How else would you know
what the hell I chose?

46:24.740 --> 46:26.742
When Round 12 began,

46:27.576 --> 46:29.119
you were at negative eight points.

46:29.786 --> 46:31.413
I was at negative nine points.

46:31.997 --> 46:34.333
Even if you messed up,
you'd still have another chance.

46:34.917 --> 46:37.294
So, instead of going for the win,

46:37.878 --> 46:40.130
you bet that he and I
would invalidate each other.

46:40.756 --> 46:44.468
So I figured
you would choose a random number.

46:45.260 --> 46:48.430
But what are the chances
you'd get it right? Are you a psychic?

46:48.514 --> 46:52.893
If he and I invalidate each other,
you thought we'd choose from the first 50.

46:54.645 --> 46:56.396
He predicted my exact thoughts.

46:57.814 --> 47:01.818
At the start of the round, the King
had more than a three-point lead over him.

47:09.368 --> 47:11.119
If I chose the same as the King,

47:11.203 --> 47:12.955
I couldn't make up
the three-point difference.

47:17.751 --> 47:22.005
But if they chose the same numbers,
I thought I might win.

47:27.261 --> 47:29.263
So you avoided choosing from the first 50.

47:30.764 --> 47:32.015
If you're going to run away,

47:32.599 --> 47:35.102
then it's only natural
that you want to run far.

47:36.103 --> 47:40.440
But even so, 90 to 100 is too extreme
and doesn't feel right.

47:41.024 --> 47:42.651
So you avoided those too.

47:43.235 --> 47:48.031
Any doubles are too obvious,
so you avoided those as well.

47:48.615 --> 47:52.035
The same goes for 60 and 70
and any easy numbers like that.

47:52.536 --> 47:55.998
The numbers that people
often choose on a whim,

47:56.081 --> 47:57.916
that is, 3, 5, and 8, were also out.

47:58.500 --> 47:59.751
All prime numbers were also out.

48:00.669 --> 48:02.170
It became easy after that.

48:03.297 --> 48:08.885
Lastly, any numbers you often see in life
that can be easily imagined were out.

48:09.761 --> 48:11.096
A game console.

48:11.805 --> 48:12.806
A movie title.

48:13.432 --> 48:14.433
A brand logo.

48:15.684 --> 48:20.230
Then what we have left is either 62 or 74.

48:20.897 --> 48:22.399
That's as far as I could get.

48:24.067 --> 48:25.569
After that,

48:26.695 --> 48:27.529
it was just luck.

48:29.698 --> 48:32.659
I should have chosen 74.

48:34.995 --> 48:38.206
There is a participant
who has negative ten points.

48:40.000 --> 48:40.834
No…

48:41.335 --> 48:42.919
No…

48:43.003 --> 48:44.546
No!

48:45.714 --> 48:48.050
No…

48:51.053 --> 48:52.638
No!

48:53.263 --> 48:54.097
No!

49:07.569 --> 49:08.445
You know…

49:10.405 --> 49:15.577
She said that the value
of everyone's life isn't equal.

49:17.496 --> 49:21.667
I wonder if she still thought that
just before she died.

49:26.004 --> 49:27.172
Have you

49:28.715 --> 49:32.219
seen the underside of this world
with your own eyes?

49:35.263 --> 49:39.351
Infants die because they can't get
antidiarrheics that cost mere pennies.

49:40.936 --> 49:44.439
Little girls are sold
to pay off their parents' debts.

49:47.109 --> 49:50.320
All the people who can't escape
the never-ending cycle of poverty.

49:55.158 --> 49:57.244
A new rule will be added.

49:57.911 --> 49:59.287
ADDITIONAL RULES

49:59.371 --> 50:04.710
When someone chooses zero,
whoever chooses 100 will be the winner.

50:07.796 --> 50:09.005
I see.

50:09.589 --> 50:12.843
Since the result is always
the average multiplied by 0.8,

50:13.510 --> 50:18.014
as long as there are just two of us,
whoever chooses the lower number will win.

50:19.057 --> 50:23.895
In other words, if you keep choosing zero,
you'll win for sure.

50:25.272 --> 50:29.151
But thanks to this new rule,
everything is fair now.

50:30.986 --> 50:32.904
If one of us chooses zero,

50:32.988 --> 50:36.074
then the other will win
if they choose 100.

50:36.992 --> 50:41.037
But if a person predicts
that will happen and chooses 100,

50:41.538 --> 50:44.541
then the other person will choose 1.

50:45.876 --> 50:49.796
Those are the only three choices
if you want to win this game.

50:50.547 --> 50:54.551
Now it's a fair and simple game

50:55.051 --> 50:57.721
that's a toss-up between zero, 1, and 100.

51:00.849 --> 51:06.021
But I can't choose the same number
as you even once if I want to win.

51:08.690 --> 51:10.859
I'm still in a difficult bind.

51:13.111 --> 51:14.279
ROUND 13

51:14.988 --> 51:15.947
You know,

51:16.990 --> 51:18.992
you seem desperate to make things fair.

51:20.410 --> 51:22.412
What's making you do that?

51:25.957 --> 51:27.042
Tell me…

51:28.001 --> 51:30.921
If you had one million doses
of a life-saving vaccine,

51:32.672 --> 51:34.925
which one million people would you save?

51:37.302 --> 51:38.303
I see.

51:39.346 --> 51:40.680
Now I understand.

51:42.557 --> 51:47.145
It's not that you're trying
to measure the value of life.

51:47.813 --> 51:50.816
You don't want
to have to decide the value of life.

51:51.983 --> 51:55.904
Yes. I don't know what makes
one life more valuable than another.

51:56.822 --> 52:01.493
A life that's worth saving
and a life that is not…

52:02.577 --> 52:04.162
What is the difference between the two?

52:06.915 --> 52:10.335
So, how would you answer my question?

52:12.045 --> 52:15.048
I'd very much like to hear
the answer from someone like you.

52:16.800 --> 52:19.970
I'd give them to children
without parents or money.

52:22.931 --> 52:23.932
How unexpected.

52:24.015 --> 52:25.600
That would be ideal.

52:26.434 --> 52:28.228
But it's ultimately money that talks.

52:28.812 --> 52:29.855
If you've got money,

52:30.397 --> 52:33.733
then it's very easy
to end the lives of poor children.

52:35.151 --> 52:39.823
I know you've seen that world
with your own eyes, haven't you?

52:39.906 --> 52:40.907
Yes, I have.

52:42.033 --> 52:44.536
Since a certain company
wouldn't pay a settlement,

52:45.370 --> 52:48.373
people died because
they couldn't receive proper treatment.

52:48.456 --> 52:50.292
Then you know

52:51.334 --> 52:53.837
that there's no such thing
as fairness or equality in this world.

52:53.920 --> 52:54.963
Because there isn't…

52:57.340 --> 52:59.175
Isn't that why we should fight?

53:24.409 --> 53:26.328
There.

53:28.204 --> 53:29.497
It'll be next week.

53:30.081 --> 53:31.041
Hang in there.

53:38.214 --> 53:39.382
Doctor.

53:41.551 --> 53:42.969
Thank you so much.

53:43.053 --> 53:44.054
Not at all.

53:46.264 --> 53:47.724
- I'll be going now.
- Goodbye.

53:59.527 --> 54:02.614
Hayato's condition has stabilized,

54:02.697 --> 54:04.741
so this operation should save him.

54:05.575 --> 54:07.327
I need to talk to you about that.

54:07.827 --> 54:11.039
The waiting list order
for transplants has changed.

54:11.665 --> 54:13.917
- The order has changed?
- Yes.

54:18.630 --> 54:20.382
This patient will get a transplant first.

54:25.178 --> 54:26.012
REFERRAL

54:26.096 --> 54:27.597
The grandson of a friend of the director.

54:27.681 --> 54:28.598
DAIKI TAKAHASHI
ADDRESS: SETAGAYA CITY, TOKYO

54:28.682 --> 54:30.684
- Then what about Hayato?
- He'll get his later.

54:32.310 --> 54:33.561
They're a big financial donor.

54:34.729 --> 54:36.815
That's how
this university hospital survives.

54:40.235 --> 54:41.236
It can't be helped.

54:42.028 --> 54:44.531
Everything has
an order of importance in this world.

54:45.907 --> 54:48.493
You explain things
to that patient's parents.

54:49.995 --> 54:50.996
What reason should I give?

54:54.749 --> 54:56.001
Think of one.

54:56.501 --> 54:57.669
You're his physician, right?

55:21.067 --> 55:21.901
Well…

55:23.153 --> 55:25.238
Even if he could've gotten
a transplant last week,

55:25.822 --> 55:27.323
he probably would've died anyway.

55:31.036 --> 55:32.370
Don't hold it against me.

55:33.455 --> 55:37.459
To save people's lives,
you have to abandon your ideals.

55:43.298 --> 55:44.466
I don't mind.

55:46.426 --> 55:48.428
It doesn't bother me at all.

55:51.473 --> 55:52.891
It's part of the job.

56:02.150 --> 56:03.610
KINKI CHUO MEDICAL CENTER

56:09.407 --> 56:10.742
SAKURAZAKA UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

56:18.124 --> 56:20.251
PHYSICIAN
PEDIATRIC CARDIOVASCULAR SURGERY

56:27.342 --> 56:28.927
Take care of it.

56:29.511 --> 56:30.345
Got it.

56:44.275 --> 56:45.610
Very interesting.

56:48.363 --> 56:50.657
I think I may have come to this land

56:51.449 --> 56:53.159
just so I could play this game with you.

56:59.541 --> 57:00.959
I'm choosing 100.

57:07.257 --> 57:08.424
What are you up to?

57:09.592 --> 57:11.094
A little assistance.

57:12.804 --> 57:13.721
Are you insane?

57:14.848 --> 57:16.266
If I know you'll choose 100,

57:16.766 --> 57:20.103
the only way
you can survive is if I choose zero!

57:24.482 --> 57:25.733
Mine is a life

57:26.860 --> 57:29.279
that is charging headlong toward death.

57:30.989 --> 57:34.993
Does this life have value or not?

57:36.244 --> 57:37.745
I'd like for you to decide.

58:23.124 --> 58:25.293
Why have you done all this?

58:28.129 --> 58:30.465
We live in a ludicrous world.

58:35.720 --> 58:37.680
If we abandon our ideals, it's all over.

58:46.564 --> 58:47.524
Ideals?

59:07.126 --> 59:08.294
Let's go.

59:09.212 --> 59:11.673
Forget me. You get going.

59:11.756 --> 59:12.966
I can't do that.

59:13.466 --> 59:17.178
In the last game I was in,
I was saved by a young man.

59:17.971 --> 59:20.723
So now it's my turn to help someone else.

59:23.226 --> 59:24.644
I won't regret it.

59:25.395 --> 59:27.146
This is my way of living.

59:30.942 --> 59:32.527
Your way of living?

59:34.487 --> 59:35.572
Let's go together.

01:00:00.805 --> 01:00:02.515
Time has expired.

01:00:03.099 --> 01:00:05.101
Here are the results for Round 13.

01:00:06.769 --> 01:00:08.938
The winner is Chishiya.

01:00:14.444 --> 01:00:16.529
Did you seriously choose zero?

01:00:25.788 --> 01:00:28.458
Round 14 will now start.

01:00:47.268 --> 01:00:49.354
The winner is Chishiya.

01:01:01.407 --> 01:01:03.826
Each of us has only one point left.

01:01:04.327 --> 01:01:05.745
The next round will be the last one.

01:01:11.793 --> 01:01:14.170
Round 15 will now start.

01:01:19.676 --> 01:01:20.760
How about it?

01:01:21.678 --> 01:01:22.845
Can you decide?

01:01:27.183 --> 01:01:29.519
If you won't decide for yourself,

01:01:30.395 --> 01:01:31.896
then just kill me.

01:01:32.689 --> 01:01:34.524
That's a fair rule, right?

01:01:36.484 --> 01:01:38.569
You think I am unable to decide.

01:01:39.904 --> 01:01:45.410
Was that the reason
why you lured me into this tie?

01:01:47.412 --> 01:01:48.496
I simply…

01:01:50.331 --> 01:01:51.582
want to know…

01:01:53.501 --> 01:01:55.628
what the last number you choose will be.

01:02:12.186 --> 01:02:15.189
If you choose 1, you will win.

01:02:28.995 --> 01:02:29.829
Momoka.

01:02:32.123 --> 01:02:34.792
I'd like you to answer just a question.

01:02:36.711 --> 01:02:41.549
You asked to play the role of the Witch
and take your own life.

01:02:47.847 --> 01:02:49.182
What was your reason?

01:02:51.517 --> 01:02:52.769
For my ideals.

01:02:57.899 --> 01:03:00.067
People have beautiful hearts,

01:03:02.111 --> 01:03:04.113
and life is precious.

01:03:04.906 --> 01:03:06.574
I believe in those things.

01:03:09.744 --> 01:03:11.579
It's because I have those ideals

01:03:12.079 --> 01:03:15.625
that I've been able to survive
in this ludicrous world.

01:03:21.798 --> 01:03:24.050
I will die as the Witch

01:03:26.719 --> 01:03:28.805
not because I lost to your rules.

01:03:31.849 --> 01:03:34.435
I did it to show you
that things won't go your way

01:03:35.937 --> 01:03:38.773
and that there won't be a massacre.

01:03:47.031 --> 01:03:49.450
If my life's going to end here
sometime anyway,

01:03:51.744 --> 01:03:54.330
then I want it to end
while proving my ideals.

01:04:01.212 --> 01:04:02.547
I don't understand

01:04:04.298 --> 01:04:08.803
the value of life or its meaning.

01:04:12.682 --> 01:04:14.350
I'm sure

01:04:15.685 --> 01:04:17.937
I won't be able to make that decision
in the future either.

01:04:21.858 --> 01:04:23.943
But what I need to decide now is…

01:04:50.177 --> 01:04:52.096
Here are the results for Round 15.

01:04:58.269 --> 01:04:59.770
I see you've decided

01:05:01.564 --> 01:05:05.818
that determining the value of life
isn't your decision.

01:05:11.657 --> 01:05:13.242
For my ideals.

01:05:16.329 --> 01:05:18.581
The winner is Chishiya.

01:05:22.376 --> 01:05:25.630
There is a participant
who has negative ten points.

01:05:26.130 --> 01:05:29.300
The game is over for this participant.

01:05:34.055 --> 01:05:36.557
What happened to your usual wry look?

01:05:38.142 --> 01:05:39.393
At last,

01:05:44.273 --> 01:05:46.025
I think I've been able to…

01:05:48.152 --> 01:05:49.904
decide how I want to live.

01:06:05.336 --> 01:06:06.754
It's thanks to you.

01:06:19.976 --> 01:06:22.645
It's now time for our turn.

01:06:28.693 --> 01:06:29.694
Oh, my.

01:06:31.112 --> 01:06:32.530
You're not up for it?

01:06:36.075 --> 01:06:38.411
At the very least,
I want the game that I run

01:06:40.496 --> 01:06:41.998
to be fair.

01:07:17.783 --> 01:07:19.785
It feels kind of unfair.

01:07:20.411 --> 01:07:22.580
It's like you won and quit on me.

01:07:24.915 --> 01:07:26.751
I envy you.

01:08:04.663 --> 01:08:08.918
GAME CLEARED
CONGRATULATIONS

01:09:07.560 --> 01:09:08.727
I wouldn't be surprised…

01:09:10.896 --> 01:09:12.565
if we die soon.

01:09:16.235 --> 01:09:17.153
But…

01:09:18.445 --> 01:09:20.781
it's a miracle
we've made it this far anyway.

01:09:25.286 --> 01:09:27.288
Since we have made it this far,

01:09:29.165 --> 01:09:30.916
no matter what happens, let's fight…

01:09:33.878 --> 01:09:34.712
to the very end.

01:09:37.631 --> 01:09:38.549
Right.

01:10:11.624 --> 01:10:13.459
I'll make it back, I swear.

01:11:04.134 --> 01:11:06.887
For my future self.

01:13:48.048 --> 01:13:53.053
Subtitle translation by: Brian Athey
